{"t":1792583195,"office":"LWX","station":"KDCA","point":"38.8894,-77.0352","field":"38.9429,-76.5684","field_station":"KNAK","afd":{"id":"14fb452a-e9d0-4e3b-9622-418fb910e32d","office":"LWX","issuanceTime":"2026-10-21T07:02:00+00:00","productText":"\n000\nFXUS61 KLWX 210702\nAFDLWX\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Baltimore MD/Washington DC\n302 AM EDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\n.WHAT HAS CHANGED...\nNo changes were made to the forecast overnight. \n\n&&\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n- 1) Dry conditions and seasonable temperatures are expected\n  through early next week.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry conditions and seasonable temperatures are expected\nthrough early next week.\n\nSurface high pressure continues to build north of the forecast \narea through the end of the week, yielding dry conditions, \nseasonal temperatures, and limited cloud cover. High \ntemperatures will be in the 60s to near 70s each day with \novernight lows in the 30s to mid 40s. \n\nHigh pressure will build southward out of southeastern Canada and \neastern Great Lakes region Saturday through Tuesday. Dry conditions \nare expected each day. There could be some areas of frost Saturday \nmorning. Temperatures will start out chilly Saturday with highs 5 to \n7 degrees below average and highs generally in the upper 50s to \nlower 60s. By Sunday, temperatures will be more seasonable. Monday \nwill encounter highs approaching or reaching the 70 degree mark. By \nTuesday, temperatures may be knocked down to seasonable once again. \nHighs in the middle 60s.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION /06Z WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nVFR conditions continue as surface high pressure builds overhead\nand dry conditions persist. Winds remain primarily out of the\nnorth today before shifting to northwesterly on Thursday. On\nFriday, winds shift to northeasterly. Terminals located near the\nI-95 corridor will gust around 15 knots each afternoon. \nOtherwise, terminals can expect light northerly winds, no \nprecipitation, and VFR conditions. \n\nVFR conditions Saturday through Sunday night. Winds light and \nvariable through the period.\n\n&&\n\n.MARINE...\nThe Nor'easter off the Mid-Atlantic coast will deliver a \nprolonged period of SCA conditions (mainly over the \ncentral/lower waters). Small Craft Advisories remain in effect\nand will likely need to be extended. The threat is highest in \nthe lower portions of the waters, with additional Advisories \npossible through the end of the week. Otherwise, dry conditions \nand non-hazardous marine weather is expected. \n\nNo marine hazards expected Saturday through Sunday night. Winds \nlight and variable through the period.\n\n&&\n\n.TIDES/COASTAL FLOODING...\nA Nor'easter will continue to circulate offshore through\nThursday as high pressure builds to our north. This will lead to\npersistent northerly flow over the waters. Minor flooding is\nexpected at many tidal sites tonight through the day Thursday, \nbut some uncertainty still remains.\n\n&&\n\n.LWX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...\nDC...None.\nMD...Small Craft Advisory until 6 PM EDT this evening for MDZ008.\n     Coastal Flood Advisory until 4 AM EDT early this morning for \n     MDZ014.\nVA...None.\nWV...None.\nMARINE...Small Craft Advisory until 6 PM EDT this evening for \n     ANZ530>534-537>543.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...AVS/KLW\nAVIATION...AVS/KLW\nMARINE...AVS/KLW\n"},"forecast":{"t":1792583146,"days":{"2026-10-21":{"hi":65,"lo":44,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-22":{"hi":66,"lo":46,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-23":{"hi":61,"lo":40,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-24":{"hi":62,"lo":41,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-25":{"hi":65,"lo":44,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-26":{"hi":69,"lo":49,"pop":0,"short":"Sunny"},"2026-10-27":{"hi":68,"lo":49,"pop":0,"short":"Mostly Sunny"}}},"grid":{"t0":1792580400,"n":48,"ceil":[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null